# CODEOWNERS identifies the owner for Phase A gate files.
#
# This file does not enforce review by itself. It becomes a merge control only when a
# protected-branch rule or repository ruleset requires code-owner review and prevents
# the pull-request author from satisfying that review alone. The repository variable
# IDENTITY_MODEL_V2_SHA256 is the external digest anchor; CODEOWNERS is review metadata.
#
# The checkers, CI invocation, packaging boundary, identity files, governance map, and
# session audit hook are covered so a ruleset can protect the whole gate surface.

# The trusted base: checkers, their CI invocation, and this file itself.
/scripts/                       @jeffatoney
/.github/workflows/             @jeffatoney
/.github/CODEOWNERS             @jeffatoney

# Packaging. The clean-engine boundary is "legacy/mtg_sim is not an installed package",
# which is one line of pyproject.toml away from being undone.
/pyproject.toml                 @jeffatoney

# The frozen identity model and its lock.
/docs/spec/identity/            @jeffatoney

# Governance classification.
/automation/phase-a-authority-map.json  @jeffatoney
/docs/governance/               @jeffatoney

# The guard that runs for the whole test session.
/tests/conftest.py              @jeffatoney
